Negative sampling.
Negative (non-binder) examples of TCR-pMHC reactivities are essential for evaluating predictive performance of all ML models. Such examples are additionally required for training supervised ML models, although not generative models which would require only the positive examples to learn the distribution of binders. Ideal data would include the experimentally confirmed non-binder TCR-pMHC pairs sampled from the same TCR and pMHC distributions as the positive examples. Such experimental negative examples are very rare in publicly available data. Some publications on TCR-pMHC specificity modeling use internally generated undisclosed datasets
19
. Most publications impute the negative examples by randomly pairing TCRs and pMHCs from the positive examples
10
,
12
,
13
